\begin_layout Subsubsection
For a general function 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

 , 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}$
\end_inset

 is twice its average
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
By definition:
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Box Boxed
position "t"
hor_pos "c"
has_inner_box 1
inner_pos "t"
use_parbox 0
use_makebox 0
width "100col%"
special "none"
height "1in"
height_special "totalheight"
thickness "0.4pt"
separation "3pt"
shadowsize "4pt"
framecolor "black"
backgroundcolor "yellow"
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
f_{avg}:=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}f(x)dx=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}f(x)dx\right)=\frac{1}{2}a_{0}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
The ODE derived for 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}$
\end_inset

 determines the FP and rat of convergence
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
We've computed the equation for 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}$
\end_inset

 and the fixed point derived by it:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\dot{a_{0}} & =\left(\frac{J}{2}-1\right)a_{0}+2\\
a_{0}^{*} & =\frac{4}{2-J}
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\begin_inset Box Boxed
position "t"
hor_pos "c"
has_inner_box 1
inner_pos "t"
use_parbox 0
use_makebox 0
width "100col%"
special "none"
height "1in"
height_special "totalheight"
thickness "0.4pt"
separation "3pt"
shadowsize "4pt"
framecolor "black"
backgroundcolor "yellow"
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
From this we can tell that when 
\begin_inset Formula $J\nearrow2$
\end_inset

 , the value of 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(2-J\right)\searrow0$
\end_inset

 and thus 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}^{*}\nearrow\infty$
\end_inset

.
 I.e.
 the average firing rate at the FP would be greater.
 Also, when 
\begin_inset Formula $J\nearrow2$
\end_inset

, the value of 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(\frac{J}{2}-1\right)\nearrow0$
\end_inset

.
 I.e.
 the rate of change for the average firing rate is greater.
 Eventually, when 
\begin_inset Formula $2<J$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $0<\left(\frac{J}{2}-1\right)$
\end_inset

 and the average firing rate goes to infinity
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
\begin_inset Formula $J=2.1$
\end_inset

 Only 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}$
\end_inset

 diverges
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
As showed in 1.4, the 
\begin_inset Formula $b_{n}$
\end_inset

's are always 0.
 The 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{n}$
\end_inset

's converge when 
\begin_inset Formula $J<\pi$
\end_inset

 but if 
\begin_inset Formula $2<J$
\end_inset

 then 
\begin_inset Formula $a_{0}$
\end_inset

 diverges.
 
